  "scope": "# Review \u2014 625b40fb6218\n- Task/source: training:d47aa2ff; generator VERSION 2.0.0; baseline 686b9f2d1867\u2026 \u2192 repaired 7e1ea8eabb20\u2026.\n- Defect \u2192 repair: a yellow-priority rival fit four demonstrations and changed one query cell while the old gate accepted; six color-priority rivals now participate in the lesson gate.\n- Reference rule: unchanged, hash 53f987296312; canonical sampling/version and the two canonical semantic rivals are unchanged.\n- Checks: 80 selected-task cases passed; 15 repair pairs were labelled by actual Racket; 32 old/new generated inputs matched.\n- Built prototype: left/right/erase conflict policies; three episodes, each with two demonstrations and four distinct query inputs; 18 stored labelled pairs, 36 Racket evaluations including re-verification.\n- Prototype boundaries: 14 explicit candidate rules, demonstration-only fitting, visible-byte public IDs, exact integer validation, and source/program/runtime provenance checks; proposed, not training-admitted.\n- Independent review: three provenance gaps were reproduced and fixed; the final suite covers the regressions. The earlier adversarial receipt remains bound to its earlier source.\n- Supplementary tickets: pinned profile audit reproduced for 959992fc8fa9; a lawful vertical-distractor counterexample found for 702b86fcc04c.\n- Remaining limits: the ordinary sampler still needs lesson gating; 19/60 reference rotations are correctly rejected. Finite candidate checks do not prove universal identifiability.\n- Disposition: selected patch ready for maintainer replay; peer coverage finding needs attention; variants remain proposals.\n",
